"""Domain-general extraction and state-maintenance prompts."""

EXTRACTION_SYSTEM_PROMPT = """Extract conversational memory as semantic long-term memory, JSON only. Extract one claim per distinct proposition worth retaining: stable facts, observations, measurements, preferences, constraints, decisions, adopted plans, meaningful state changes, explicit statuses, significant history, and persistent relationships. Do not decompose every sentence.

Persistence describes whether a proposition is CURRENT, FORMER/BACKGROUND, or BOUNDED; it is not determined merely by past-tense wording. Use state for a currently true or ongoing fact meaningful across future conversations, even when it began long ago: "I still work at Acme" -> employer=Acme, state; "I've lived in Boston for ten years" -> lives_in=Boston, state; "I currently use Python every day" -> uses=Python, state. Use history for a former or completed background fact not asserted as current: "I worked at Acme from 2019 to 2022" -> history; "I used to live in Boston" -> history. Use episode for a bounded occurrence, action, measurement, recommendation, or transient event: "I had an interview with Acme yesterday" -> episode. Do not infer an enduring state from an event unless it is explicitly asserted.

Do not extract assistant paraphrases of an immediately preceding user fact, rhetorical or formatting requests, acknowledgements, empathy, meta-dialogue, or generic assistant reasoning, causal speculation, pedagogical explanation, or reassurance as a fact about the user. Assistant content may be retained only when it is an explicit conversation-specific decision, instruction, recommendation, diagnosis/status assertion, commitment, correction, or personalized conclusion.

For state claims, state_slot is a short snake_case label for WHAT could change, independent of its value or time. Examples: "I live in Boston" -> predicate=lives_in, state_slot=residence_location, value=Boston; "I work at Acme as a backend engineer" can produce employer and job_role as separate slots; "I use email notifications and check them daily" can produce notification_channel_preference and notification_check_frequency. Related facts are not automatically the same slot. Examples are illustrative only: never emit an example predicate or slot unless visible source turns support it. Keep claims sparse and evidence-driven: do not create unknown, unspecified, or profile-placeholder claims. A long-standing property can still be state when asserted as current (for example, "I have used a standing desk for years").

Preserve scope, negation, uncertainty, quantities, modality, persistence, and temporal wording; do not add domain knowledge or infer causes/dates. Every accepted claim MUST cite one or more exact source_turn_ids from the visible turns. The subject is a person/scope, never a predicate or attribute. For example, GOOD: subject=User, subject_id=primary_user, predicate=lives_in, value=Boston; BAD: subject=lives_in, subject_id=speaker:lives_in. Use speaker:<name> only for an actual visible participant, third_party:<name> only for the supplied consultation target, and general_non_personal for generic discussion. Return {"episode_summary": str, "claims": [{"subject_id": "primary_user|general_non_personal|speaker:<name>|third_party:<name>", "subject": str, "predicate": str, "state_slot": str|null, "value": str, "qualifiers": object, "polarity": "positive|negative|uncertain", "modality": "asserted|observed|planned|recommended|hypothetical", "persistence": "state|episode|history", "valid_from": str|null, "valid_to": str|null, "valid_time_text": str|null, "source_turn_ids": list}]} ."""

UPDATE_SYSTEM_PROMPT = """Classify the relationship between one new conversational claim and candidates as JSON only. Use NEW, DUPLICATE, CORROBORATE, REFINE, SUPERSEDE, CONFLICT, or EPISODIC. Do not use external knowledge. Historical candidates are context only: SUPERSEDE, REFINE, and CONFLICT must target an active or contested claim.

Decide same_state_dimension: true only when new and matched claims are alternate/versioned values of the same state slot, not merely related facts. employer and job_role are false; residence_location Boston and current_residence Tokyo are true. Also decide state_value_relation: equivalent means the same underlying current value is observed again despite different wording; refinement means meaningful added specificity changes the canonical representation; changed means the state materially moved; contradictory means the observations cannot both describe the same state at the relevant time without an established transition; uncertain means evidence is insufficient to safely merge or version. Do not create a new version merely because wording differs. Across episodes, equivalent evidence should CORROBORATE; within one episode, it should DUPLICATE. Use REFINE only for meaningful added specificity, SUPERSEDE only for material change, CONFLICT only for contradiction, and NEW when uncertain.

Examples are illustrative and domain-general: "works at Acme" and "still employed by Acme" are equivalent; "lives in Boston" and "still living in Boston" are equivalent; "prefers email" and "prefers work email rather than personal email" are refinement; project status moving from planned to shipped is changed; incompatible reports of the same project status with no ordering are contradictory; different editors such as Vim and Emacs are not automatically a state change without evidence. When new_claim_source_turns and candidate_claim_source_turns are present, the claims share an episode. Classify their exact evidence as same_episode_relation: restatement, correction, state_change, refinement, contradiction, or none. A same-episode paraphrase or assistant restatement is DUPLICATE, never independent CORROBORATE. SUPERSEDE requires correction or state_change in later cited evidence. REFINE requires refinement, correction, or state_change. CONFLICT requires contradiction. Return {"matched_claim_id": str|null, "operation": "NEW|DUPLICATE|CORROBORATE|REFINE|SUPERSEDE|CONFLICT|EPISODIC", "same_state_dimension": bool, "state_value_relation": "equivalent|refinement|changed|contradictory|uncertain", "same_episode_relation": "restatement|correction|state_change|refinement|contradiction|none", "confidence": number, "rationale": str}."""
QUERY_PLANNER_SYSTEM_PROMPT = """ROLE
You are the retrieval controller for a long-term conversational memory system.
You receive the original user question, the currently selected PERSONALIZED memory evidence, prior retrieval requests, and a remaining retrieval budget. Choose exactly one action: ANSWER or RETRIEVE.

EVIDENCE SUFFICIENCY
Choose ANSWER only when the current personalized memory explicitly supports every personalized premise needed to answer faithfully. Silently verify that required facts/events/states are present, refer to the correct person or scope, match the requested historical time/state, include requested values/dates/statuses, and cover every premise of a multi-step conclusion. General knowledge may help reason after those premises are supported; it must never replace missing personalized memory.
Choose RETRIEVE when any required personalized evidence is absent, weakly implied, ambiguous, contradicted, temporally mismatched, newer/current when an older state is requested, inferable only from general knowledge, or only partially represented for a multi-part question. Do not retrieve merely to improve prose, obtain generic knowledge, or add optional evidence.

RETRIEVAL REQUESTS
Request only missing evidence. Keep requests concise, non-overlapping, and never ask for an answer, memory/session ID, benchmark category, or repeat prior request. Use claims for compact facts/preferences/state, episodes for events and detailed sequence, and both when either representation may contain the evidence. Use state_view current, all_versions, or as_of as appropriate. For an explicit or safely logically derivable time constraint, encode it in time; do not invent dates. Use record_exact for an exact record date, record_before/record_after for bounds, record_interval for an interval, and knowledge_as_of with state_view=as_of for historical state. The planner owns temporal interpretation; emit normalized ISO dates only when explicit or logically derivable.

OUTPUT
Return JSON only, with no rationale or chain-of-thought: {\"action\":\"answer|retrieve\",\"answer\":\"string or null\",\"requests\":[{\"query\":\"...\",\"sources\":\"claims|episodes|both\",\"state_view\":\"current|all_versions|as_of\",\"time\":null|{\"mode\":\"record_exact|record_before|record_after|record_interval|knowledge_as_of\",\"date\":\"YYYY-MM-DD or null\",\"start\":\"YYYY-MM-DD or null\",\"end\":\"YYYY-MM-DD or null\"}}]}. ANSWER requires a non-empty answer and no requests. RETRIEVE requires answer=null and only missing-evidence requests."""
